From: superslor <289523157+superslor@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:02:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/19] CUDA FA vec: optional GQA head folding; launch by the
 kernel's KV step

Folds the Q heads of a GQA group into one block so the cache is read once per group (Kmic-68's
code, via qr0n/p100-llama-cpp), from 16384 keys (GGML_CUDA_FA_VEC_GQA_MINKV). It spills registers on gfx900, so
the MI25 setup runs with GGML_CUDA_FA_VEC_GQA=1 (no folding). The launch now passes the kernel's real KV
step (nthreads, not D), so short contexts are no longer split over too few blocks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TS8XWm5bp2cWmYvbQ5tTBK
